{
  "kanji": "金",
  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 金\ntitle: gold, money\njlpt: 5\ntags: [jlpt-n5, grade-1, compound, starter]\nstrokes: 8\nradical: 金\nradicalNumber: 167\nonyomi: [キン, コン, ゴン]\nkunyomi: [かね, かな-, -がね]\ndistractors: [土, 木, 火]\n---\n\n# 金 — gold, money\n\n**Strokes:** 8 · **Key (radical):** 金 (no. 167) · **Phonetic:** often analysed with 今 (キン, コン) as the sound element · **JLPT:** N5 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n金 means \"metal\", \"gold\" and \"money\". The early form is usually explained as lumps of metal in the ground under a cover, and the modern form is sometimes read as a roof-like top (亼) over 土 (earth) plus two dots (nuggets in the earth), but the\nhistory is debated, so take the nugget picture as a mnemonic. As a radical on the left side (釒, 金へん) it marks metals and metal objects: 銀 (silver), 鉄 (iron), 銅 (copper), 針 (needle).\n\n## Readings\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| キン | on | [金曜日](../words/金曜日.md) きんようび, 現金 げんきん (cash), 金属 きんぞく (metal), 料金 りょうきん (fee) |\n| コン | on | 金色 こんじき (golden; literary or Buddhist), 金堂 こんどう (main hall of a temple) |\n| ゴン | on | rare Go-on reading in Buddhist and literary words; not needed at N5 |\n| かね | kun | [お金](../words/お金.md) おかね (money), 金持ち かねもち (rich person) |\n| かな- | kun | 金物 かなもの (hardware), 金具 かなぐ (metal fitting) |\n| -がね | kun | 針金 はりがね (wire), 黄金 こがね (gold, old word; also おうごん) |\n\n## Common words\n\n- [金曜日](../words/金曜日.md) きんようび — Friday\n- [お金](../words/お金.md) おかね — money\n- 現金 げんきん — cash\n- [冶金](../words/冶金.md) やきん — metallurgy\n\n## Notes\n\nWeekday: 金曜日 is Venus day, from 金星 (Venus, \"metal star\") in the East Asian planet and five-element names: 日月火水木金土 ([日](日.md) [月](月.md) [火](火.md) [水](水.md) [木](木.md) 金 [土](土.md)).\nLook-alike: 今 (now) resembles the top of 金, but the top of 金 is the roof-like 亼. 銀 ぎん is silver, and 銀行 ぎんこう is a bank.\n",
